    "audioUrl": "NCE/NCE1/143&144.A Walk Through the Woods.mp3",
    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE1/143&144.A Walk Through the Woods.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第一册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:A Walk Through the Woods]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:00.95]Lesson 143 | 第143课\n[00:03.87]A walk through the woods | 林中散步\n[00:07.33]Listen to the tape then answer this question. | 听录音，然后回答这个问题。\n[00:12.86]What was so funny about the words on the sign? | 牌子上的字有什么好笑的？\n[00:19.84]I live in a very old town which is surrounded by beautiful woods. | 我住在一个非常古老的小镇，它被美丽的树林环绕着。\n[00:28.00]It is a famous beauty spot. | 这是一个著名的风景区。\n[00:32.06]On Sundays, hundreds of people come from the city to see our town and to walk through the woods. | 每到星期天，成百上千的人从城里赶来参观我们的小镇，并在树林中散步。\n[00:42.50]Visitors have been asked to keep the woods clean and tidy. | 游客们被要求保持树林的清洁整齐。\n[00:49.55]Litter baskets have been placed under the trees, but people still throw their rubbish everywhere. | 树下放置了垃圾筐，但人们仍然随处乱扔垃圾。\n[00:58.99]Last Wednesday, I went for a walk in the woods. | 上个星期三，我到树林里散步。\n[01:05.51]What I saw made me very sad. | 我看到的一切让我很难过。\n[01:10.74]I counted seven old cars and three old refrigerators. | 我数出了七辆旧汽车和三台旧冰箱。\n[01:18.12]The little baskets were empty and the ground was covered with pieces of paper, | 那些垃圾筐都是空的，地上却铺满了碎纸片，\n[01:25.80]cigarette ends, old tyres, empty bottles and rusty tins. | 烟头、旧轮胎、空瓶子和生锈的罐头盒。\n[01:34.49]Among the rubbish, I found a sign which said, 'Anyone who leaves litter in these woods will be prosecuted!' | 在这些垃圾中，我发现了一个牌子，上面写着：“凡在此树林中乱扔垃圾者，将受到起诉！”",
