    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:A Private Conversation]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:09.77]Why did the writer complain to the people behind him? | 作者为什么要向他身后的人抱怨？\n[00:15.91]Last week I went to the theatre. | 上周我去了剧院。\n[00:19.39]I had a very good seat. | 我有一个很好的座位。\n[00:22.07]The play was very interesting. | 戏很有趣。\n[00:25.10]I did not enjoy it. | 我却没有享受到乐趣。\n[00:27.43]A young man and a young woman were sitting behind me. | 一对年轻的男女坐在我身后。\n[00:31.96]They were talking loudly. | 他们大声地说着话。\n[00:34.59]I got very angry. | 我非常生气。\n[00:37.41]I could not hear the actors. | 我听不见演员的讲话。\n[00:40.64]I turned round. | 我转过身。\n[00:42.80]I looked at the man and the woman angrily. | 我怒气冲冲地看着那一男一女。\n[00:47.27]They did not pay any attention. | 他们却不理不睬。\n[00:50.69]In the end, I could not bear it. | 最后，我忍不住了。\n[00:54.98]I turned round again. | 我又转过身去。\n[00:57.75]'I can't hear a word!' I said angrily. | “我一个字也听不见了！”我生气地说。\n[01:03.45]'It's none of your business,' | “不关你的事，”\n[01:06.27]the young man said rudely. | 那个年轻人粗鲁地说。\n[01:09.00]'This is a private conversation!' | “这是私人谈话！”",
