    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:The Best and the Worst]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:09.96]Why is Joe's garden | 为什么乔的花园\n[00:12.05]the most beautiful one in the town? | 是镇上最漂亮的一个？\n[00:16.92]Joe Sanders has the most beautiful garden | 乔·桑德斯拥有最美丽的花园\n[00:20.67]in our town. | 在我们镇上。\n[00:22.27]Nearly everybody enters for | 几乎每个人都报名参加\n[00:25.17]'The Nicest Garden Competition' each year, | 每年的“最美花园竞赛”，\n[00:29.12]but Joe wins every time. | 但乔每次都赢。\n[00:32.60]Bill Frith's garden is larger than Joe's. | 比尔·弗里斯的花园比乔的花园大。\n[00:36.52]Bill works harder than Joe | 比尔比乔更努力工作\n[00:38.88]and grows more flowers and vegetables, | 并且种植更多的花卉和蔬菜，\n[00:42.12]but Joe's garden is more interesting. | 但乔的花园更有趣。\n[00:45.75]He has made neat paths | 他修建了整齐的小径\n[00:47.96]and has built a wooden bridge over a pool. | 并在池塘上架起了一座木桥。\n[00:52.25]I like gardens too, | 我也喜欢花园，\n[00:54.38]but I do not like hard work. | 但我不喜欢辛苦劳作。\n[00:57.80]Every year | 每年\n[00:59.05]I enter for the garden competition too, | 我也参加花园竞赛，\n[01:02.76]and I always win a little prize | 我总是赢得一个小奖\n[01:05.97]for the worst garden in the town! | 因为我是镇上最差的花园！",
