    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:One Good Turn Deserves Another]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.82]Who paid for Tony's dinner? | 谁付了托尼的晚餐钱？\n[00:14.36]I was having dinner at a restaurant when Tony Steele came in. | 我正在一家餐馆吃饭，这时托尼·斯蒂尔走了进来。\n[00:19.90]Tony worked in a lawyer's office years ago, | 托尼多年前在一家律师事务所工作，\n[00:23.42]but he is now working at a bank. | 但他现在在一家银行工作。\n[00:27.04]He gets a good salary, | 他薪水很高，\n[00:29.43]but he always borrows money from his friends and never pays it back. | 但他总是向朋友借钱，从不还。\n[00:35.61]Tony saw me and came and sat at the same table. | 托尼看到了我，走过来坐在同一张桌子旁。\n[00:39.94]He has never borrowed money from me. | 他从没向我借过钱。\n[00:43.19]While he was eating, I asked him to lend me twenty pounds. | 他吃饭的时候，我请他借给我二十英镑。\n[00:48.33]To my surprise, he gave me the money immediately. | 令我惊讶的是，他立刻把钱给了我。\n[00:53.78]'I have never borrowed any money from you,' | “我从没向你借过钱，”\n[00:56.77]Tony said, 'so now you can pay for my dinner!' | 托尼说，“所以现在你可以为我的晚餐付钱了！”",
