    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE2/15.Good News.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:Good News]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:09.78]What was the good news? | 好消息是什么？\n[00:13.88]The secretary told me that Mr. Harmsworth would see me. | 秘书告诉我哈姆斯沃思先生会见我。\n[00:19.28]I felt very nervous when I went into his office. | 当我走进他的办公室时，我感到非常紧张。\n[00:24.36]He did not look up from his desk when I entered. | 我进去时，他没有从办公桌上抬起头。\n[00:28.84]After I had sat down, | 我坐下后，\n[00:31.23]he said that business was very bad. | 他说生意很糟。\n[00:35.10]He told me that the firm could not afford to pay such large salaries. | 他告诉我公司负担不起支付如此高的薪水。\n[00:41.52]Twenty people had already left. | 已经有二十人离开了。\n[00:45.06]I knew that my turn had come. | 我知道轮到我了。\n[00:48.59]'Mr. Harmsworth,' I said in a weak voice. | “哈姆斯沃思先生，”我用微弱的声音说。\n[00:53.30]'Don't interrupt,' he said. | “不要打断，”他说。\n[00:56.14]Then he smiled and told me I would receive an extra thousand pounds a year! | 然后他笑了，告诉我每年将额外获得一千英镑！",
