    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:A Polite Request]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.02]What was the polite request? | 有礼貌的请求是什么？\n[00:14.64]If you park your car in the wrong place, | 如果你把车停错了地方，\n[00:18.11]a traffic policeman will soon find it. | 交通警察很快就会发现它。\n[00:21.68]You will be very lucky if he lets you go without a ticket. | 如果他让你走而不开罚单，你将非常幸运。\n[00:26.86]However, this does not always happen. | 然而，这并非总是发生。\n[00:31.48]Traffic police are sometimes very polite. | 交通警察有时非常有礼貌。\n[00:35.98]During a holiday in Sweden, | 在瑞典度假期间，\n[00:38.66]I found this note on my car: | 我在车上发现了这张字条：\n[00:42.04]'sir, we welcome you to our city. This is a No Parking area. | “先生，我们欢迎您来到我们的城市。这里是禁停区。\n[00:49.85]You will enjoy your stay here if you pay attention to our street signs. This note is only a reminder.' | 如果您注意我们的路标，您会在这里度过愉快的时光。这张字条只是一个提醒。”\n[01:00.31]If you receive a request like this, you cannot fail to obey it! | 如果你收到这样的请求，你不能不遵守它！",
