    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:Always Young]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.34]Why doesn't Aunt Jennifer tell anyone how old she is? | 珍妮弗姨妈为什么不告诉任何人她多大了？\n[00:17.39]My aunt Jennifer is an actress. | 我的珍妮弗姨妈是个演员。\n[00:20.95]She must be at least thirty-five years old. | 她肯定至少35岁了。\n[00:25.21]In spite of this, she often appears on the stage as a young girl. | 尽管如此，她还是经常在舞台上扮演一个年轻姑娘。\n[00:31.68]Jennifer will have to take part in a new play soon. | 珍妮弗很快就要参加一个新剧的演出了。\n[00:36.10]This time, she will be a girl of seventeen. | 这次，她将扮演一个17岁的姑娘。\n[00:41.18]In the play, she must appear in a bright red dress and long black stockings. | 在剧中，她必须穿一件鲜红的连衣裙和一双长长的黑丝袜。\n[00:49.17]Last year in another play, | 去年在另一个剧中，\n[00:51.70]she had to wear short socks and a bright, orange-coloured dress. | 她不得不穿短袜和一件鲜艳的橙色连衣裙。\n[00:58.45]If anyone ever asks her how old she is, | 如果有人问起她多大了，\n[01:02.55]she always answers, 'Darling, it must be terrible to be grown up!' | 她总是回答说：“亲爱的，长大成人真是太可怕了！”",
