    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:One Man in a Boat]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:11.03]Why is fishing the writer's favourite sport? | 为什么钓鱼是作者最喜欢的运动？\n[00:15.90]Fishing is my favourite sport. | 钓鱼是我最喜欢的运动。\n[00:18.88]I often fish for hours without catching anything. | 我经常钓好几个小时，却什么也钓不到。\n[00:24.11]But this does not worry me. | 但这并不困扰我。\n[00:27.65]Some fishermen are unlucky. | 有些渔夫运气不好。\n[00:30.69]Instead of catching fish, | 他们不是钓到鱼，\n[00:33.27]they catch old boots and rubbish. | 而是钓到旧靴子和垃圾。\n[00:37.33]I am even less lucky. | 我甚至更不走运。\n[00:40.24]I never catch anything -- not even old boots. | 我什么也钓不到——甚至连旧靴子都钓不到。\n[00:46.48]After having spent whole mornings on the river, | 在河上度过整个上午之后，\n[00:50.52]I always go home with an empty bag. | 我总是空手回家。\n[00:54.86]'You must give up fishing!' my friends say. 'It's a waste of time.' | “你必须放弃钓鱼！”我的朋友们说，“这简直是浪费时间。”\n[01:02.50]But they don't realize one important thing. | 但他们没有意识到一件重要的事情。\n[01:07.05]I'm not really interested in fishing. | 我对钓鱼并不真正感兴趣。\n[01:10.78]I am only interested in sitting in a boat and doing nothing at all! | 我只对坐在船上什么也不做感兴趣！",
