    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE2/22.A Glass Envelope.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:A Glass Envelope]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.79]How did Jane receive a letter from a stranger? | 简是如何收到陌生人的来信的？\n[00:16.79]My daughter, Jane, never dreamed of receiving a letter from a girl of her own age in Holland. | 我的女儿简从未想过会收到一个荷兰同龄女孩的来信。\n[00:26.87]Last year, we were travelling across the Channel and Jane put a piece of paper with her name and address on it into a bottle. | 去年，我们渡海旅行，简把一张写有她姓名和地址的纸条放进了一个瓶子里。\n[00:37.71]She threw the bottle into the sea. | 她把瓶子扔进了海里。\n[00:41.19]She never thought of it again, but ten months later, she received a letter from a girl in Holland. | 她再也没想起这件事，但十个月后，她收到了一个荷兰女孩的来信。\n[00:49.93]Both girls write to each other regularly now. | 现在两个女孩定期通信。\n[00:54.19]However, they have decided to use the post office. | 然而，她们决定使用邮局。\n[00:59.72]Letters will cost a little more, but they will certainly travel faster. | 信件会贵一点，但肯定会更快到达。",
