    "filename": "NCE2/24.It Could be Worse",
    "title": "It Could be Worse",
    "audioUrl": "NCE/NCE2/24.It Could be Worse.mp3",
    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE2/24.It Could be Worse.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:It Could be Worse]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.39]Had the writer's money been stolen? | 作者的钱被偷了吗？\n[00:15.33]I entered the hotel manager's office and sat down. | 我走进旅馆经理的办公室，坐了下来。\n[00:20.13]I had just lost ￡50 and I felt very upset. | 我刚刚丢失了50英镑，感到非常沮丧。\n[00:26.39]'I left the money in my room,' I said, 'and it's not there now. ' | “我把钱落在房间里了，”我说，“现在它不在那儿了。”\n[00:33.33]The manager was sympathetic, but he could do nothing. | 经理深表同情，但他无能为力。\n[00:38.93]'Everyone's losing money these days,' he said. | “现在大家都在丢钱，”他说。\n[00:44.08]He started to complain about this wicked world but was interrupted by a knock at the door. | 他开始抱怨这个邪恶的世界，但被一阵敲门声打断了。\n[00:52.53]A girl came in and put an envelope on his desk. | 一个女孩走了进来，在他的桌上放了一个信封。\n[00:56.98]It contained ￡50. | 里面装着50英镑。\n[00:59.97]'I found this outside this gentleman's room,' she said. | “我在这位先生的房间外面发现了这个，”她说。\n[01:05.16]'Well,' I said to the manager,'there is still some honesty in this world!' | “噢，”我对经理说，“这世界上还是有诚实可言的！”",
