    "title": "The Best Art Critics",
    "audioUrl": "NCE/NCE2/26.The Best Art Critics.mp3",
    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE2/26.The Best Art Critics.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:The Best Art Critics]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.99]Who is the student's best critic? | 谁是学生最好的评论家？\n[00:15.97]I am an art student and I paint a lot of pictures. | 我是一名艺术生，画了很多画。\n[00:21.45]Many people pretend that they understand modern art. | 许多人假装他们懂现代艺术。\n[00:26.32]They always tell you what a picture is 'about'. | 他们总是告诉你一幅画是“关于”什么的。\n[00:30.55]Of course, many pictures are not 'about' anything. | 当然，许多画根本就不是“关于”什么的。\n[00:35.30]They are just pretty patterns. | 它们只是漂亮的图案。\n[00:38.11]We like them in the same way that we like pretty curtain material. | 我们喜欢它们的方式，就像我们喜欢漂亮的窗帘布料一样。\n[00:44.18]I think that young children often appreciate modern pictures better than anyone else. | 我认为小孩子往往比任何人都更能欣赏现代画。\n[00:52.01]They notice more. | 他们注意到更多。\n[00:54.27]My sister is only seven, | 我的妹妹只有七岁，\n[00:57.08]but she always tells me whether my pictures are good or not. | 但她总是告诉我我的画好不好。\n[01:02.67]She came into my room yesterday. | 昨天她进了我的房间。\n[01:05.94]'What are you doing?' she asked. | “你在做什么？”她问。\n[01:09.36]'I'm hanging this picture on the wall,' I answered. 'It's a new one. Do you like it?' | “我正在把这幅画挂在墙上，”我回答。“这是一幅新画。你喜欢吗？”\n[01:17.48]She looked at it critically for a moment. | 她批判性地看了一会儿。\n[01:21.07]'It's all right,' she said, 'but isn't it upside down?' | “还行，”她说，“但这幅画是不是倒着挂的？”\n[01:26.93]I looked at it again. | 我又看了一遍。\n[01:28.97]She was right! It was! | 她是对的！确实是！",
