    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:No Parking]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:09.64]What is Jasper White's problem? | 贾斯珀·怀特有什么问题？\n[00:14.22]Jasper White is one of those rare people who believes in ancient myths. | 贾斯珀·怀特是那种相信古代神话的稀有人物之一。\n[00:21.12]He has just bought a new house in the city, but ever since he moved in, he has had trouble with cars and their owners. | 他刚在城里买了新房子，但自从他搬进来后，他就一直被汽车和它们的车主所困扰。\n[00:31.96]When he returns home at night, he always finds that someone has parked a car outside his gate. | 每当他晚上回家时，他总是发现有人把车停在他家门口。\n[00:40.56]Because of this, he has not been able to get his own car into his garage even once. | 因此，他甚至一次都没能把自己的车开进车库。\n[00:49.02]Jasper has put up 'No Parking' signs outside his gate, but these have not had any effect. | 贾斯珀在他家门口竖起了“禁止停车”的牌子，但这些都没有任何效果。\n[00:58.94]Now he has put an ugly stone head over the gate. | 现在他在门上放了一个丑陋的石头脑袋。\n[01:04.19]It is one of the ugliest faces I have ever seen. | 这是我见过的最丑陋的脸之一。\n[01:09.51]I asked him what it was and he told me that it was Medusa, the Gorgon. | 我问他那是什么，他告诉我那是美杜莎，那个戈尔贡女妖。\n[01:16.75]Jasper hopes that she will turn cars and their owners to stone. | 贾斯珀希望她能把汽车和它们的车主变成石头。\n[01:22.58]But none of them has been turned to stone yet! | 但他们中还没有人变成石头！",
