    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE2/42.Not Very Musical.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:Not Very Musical]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.09]What happened when the snake charmer began to play jazz? | 耍蛇人开始演奏爵士乐时发生了什么？\n[00:16.24]As we had had a long walk through one of the markets of old Delhi, | 我们在老德里的一处市场走了很长一段路之后，\n[00:22.01]we stopped at a square to have a rest. | 在一个广场停下来休息。\n[00:26.05]After a time, we noticed a snake charmer with | 过了一会儿，我们注意到广场的另一边有位耍蛇人，\n[00:29.80]two large baskets at the other side of the square, | 带着两个大篮子。\n[00:34.06]so we went to have a look at him. | 于是我们走过去看他。\n[00:37.59]As soon as he saw us, | 他一看到我们，\n[00:39.85]he picked up a long pipe which was covered with coins and opened one of the baskets. | 便拿起一根盖满硬币的长笛，打开了一个篮子。\n[00:47.11]When he began to play a tune, | 当他开始吹奏曲子时，\n[00:49.89]we had our first glimpse of the snake. | 我们第一次瞥见了那条蛇。\n[00:53.85]It rose out of the basket and began to follow the movements of the pipe. | 它从篮子里钻出来，开始跟着长笛的动作舞动。\n[01:00.19]We were very much surprised when the snake charmer | 当耍蛇人突然开始演奏爵士乐和现代流行歌曲时，\n[01:03.81]suddenly began to play jazz and modern pop songs. | 我们感到非常惊讶。\n[01:09.41]The snake, however, continued to 'dance' slowly. | 然而，那条蛇却继续缓慢地“跳舞”。\n[01:14.53]It obviously could not tell the difference between Indian music and jazz! | 它显然分辨不出印度音乐和爵士乐的区别！",
