    "id": "us/NCE2/48.Did You Want to Tell Me Something",
    "book": "us",
    "group": "NCE2",
    "filename": "NCE2/48.Did You Want to Tell Me Something",
    "title": "Did You Want to Tell Me Something",
    "audioUrl": "NCE/NCE2/48.Did You Want to Tell Me Something.mp3",
    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE2/48.Did You Want to Tell Me Something.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:Did You Want to Tell Me Something?]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:12.07]Why did the writer become very worried? | 作者为什么变得非常担心？\n[00:17.48]Dentists always ask questions when it is impossible for you to answer. | 牙医总是在你无法回答的时候问问题。\n[00:25.00]My dentist had just pulled out one of my teeth and had told me to rest for a while. | 我的牙医刚刚拔掉我的一颗牙，并让我休息一会儿。\n[00:32.31]I tried to say something, | 我试图说些什么，\n[00:34.47]but my mouth was full of cotton wool. | 但我的嘴里塞满了棉花。\n[00:38.40]He knew I collected match boxes and asked me whether my collection was growing. | 他知道我收集火柴盒，问我我的收藏是否在增加。\n[00:44.89]He then asked me how my brother was and whether I liked my new job in London. | 然后他问我哥哥怎么样，以及我是否喜欢我在伦敦的新工作。\n[00:52.98]In answer to these questions I either nodded or made strange noises. | 回答这些问题时，我不是点头就是发出奇怪的声音。\n[01:00.04]Meanwhile, my tongue was busy searching out the hole where the tooth had been. | 同时，我的舌头忙着寻找牙齿拔掉后的那个洞。\n[01:06.94]I suddenly felt very worried, but could not say anything. | 我突然感到非常担心，却什么也说不出来。\n[01:13.52]When the dentist at last removed the cotton wool from my mouth, | 当牙医最终从我嘴里取出棉花时，\n[01:18.76]I was able to tell him that he had pulled out the wrong tooth. | 我才得以告诉他他拔错了牙。",
