    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:A Pretty Carpet]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:09.89]What is the writer's carpet made of? | 作者的地毯是用什么做的？\n[00:14.42]We have just moved into a new house and I have been working hard all morning. | 我们刚搬进一所新房子，我一上午都在忙碌着。\n[00:22.27]I have been trying to get my new room in order. | 我一直想把我的新房间整理好。\n[00:27.17]This has not been easy because I own over a thousand books. | 这可不容易，因为我拥有一千多本书。\n[00:34.01]To make matters worse, | 更糟糕的是，\n[00:36.02]the room is rather small, | 房间相当小，\n[00:38.71]so I have temporarily put my books on the floor. | 所以我只好暂时把书放在地板上。\n[00:44.30]At the moment, they cover every inch of floor space | 这会儿，它们覆盖了地板上的每一寸地方，\n[00:48.83]and I actually have to walk on them to get in or out of the room. | 我实际上得踩着它们才能进出房间。\n[00:55.80]A short while ago, my sister helped me to carry one of my old bookcases up the stairs. | 不久前，我妹妹帮我把一个旧书柜搬上了楼。\n[01:04.52]She went into my room and got a big surprise when she saw all those books on the floor. | 她走进我的房间，当她看到地板上所有的书时，大吃一惊。\n[01:13.35]'This is the prettiest carpet I have ever seen,' she said. | “这是我见过的最漂亮的地毯了，”她说。\n[01:19.77]She gazed at it for some time then added, | 她凝视了一会儿，然后补充说，\n[01:24.03]'You don't need bookcases at all. | “你根本不需要书柜。\n[01:27.25]You can sit here in your spare time and read the carpet!' | 你可以在业余时间坐在这里，读读这地毯！”",
