    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:Hot Snake]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.58]What caused the fire? | 火灾是由什么引起的？\n[00:14.44]At last firemen have put out a big forest fire in California. | 消防队员终于扑灭了加利福尼亚州的一场森林大火。\n[00:21.11]Since then, they have been trying to find out how the fire began. | 从那时起，他们一直在努力查明火灾是如何开始的。\n[00:27.63]Forest fires are often caused by broken glass or by cigarette ends which people carelessly throw away. | 森林火灾通常是由碎玻璃或人们随意丢弃的烟头引起的。\n[00:37.96]Yesterday the firemen examined the ground carefully, | 昨天消防队员仔细检查了地面，\n[00:42.32]but were not able to find any broken glass. | 但没能找到任何碎玻璃。\n[00:46.80]They were also quite sure that a cigarette end did not start the fire. | 他们也相当确定不是烟头引起的火灾。\n[00:53.01]This morning, however, a firemen accidentally discovered the cause. | 然而，今天早上，一名消防队员偶然发现了起火原因。\n[00:59.38]He noticed the remains of a snake which was wound round the electric wires of a 16, 000-volt power line. | 他发现了一条缠绕在16000伏高压电线上的蛇的残骸。\n[01:09.98]In this way, he was able to solve the mystery. | 就这样，他解开了这个谜团。\n[01:14.65]The explanation was simple but very unusual. | 解释很简单，但非常不同寻常。\n[01:20.03]A bird had snatched up the snake from the ground and then dropped it on to the wires. | 一只鸟从地上抓起这条蛇，然后把它掉到了电线上。\n[01:27.83]The snake then wound itself round the wires. | 然后蛇缠绕在电线上。\n[01:31.74]When it did so, it sent sparks down to the ground and these immediately started a fire. | 当它这样做时，它向地面发出了火花，这些火花立刻引发了一场火灾。",
