    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:Sticky Fingers]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.52]What two interruptions did the writer have? | 作者遇到了哪两次打扰？\n[00:15.83]After breakfast, I sent the children to school and then I went to the shops. | 早饭后，我把孩子们送到学校，然后就去商店了。\n[00:23.02]It was still early when I returned home. | 我回到家时，时间还早。\n[00:27.30]The children were at school, my husband was at work and the house was quiet. | 孩子们在学校，我丈夫去上班了，家里很安静。\n[00:34.05]So I decided to make some meat pies. | 于是我决定做些肉馅饼。\n[00:38.34]In a short time I was busy mixing butter | 没过多久，我就忙着搅和黄油\n[00:41.82]and flour and my hands were soon covered with sticky pastry. | 和面粉，很快我的手上就沾满了黏糊糊的面团。\n[00:47.98]At exactly that moment, the telephone rang. | 就在那时，电话铃响了。\n[00:53.28]Nothing could have been more annoying. | 没有什么比这更烦人的了。\n[00:56.75]I picked up the receiver between two sticky fingers and was dismayed when I recognized the voice of Helen Bates. | 我用两根黏糊糊的手指拿起听筒，当认出海伦·贝茨的声音时，我感到很沮丧。\n[01:08.01]It took me ten minutes to persuade her to ring back later. At last I hung up the receiver. | 我花了十分钟才说服她稍后再打来。最后我挂断了电话。\n[01:17.22]What a mess! There was pastry on my fingers, on the telephone, and on the doorknobs. | 真是一团糟！我的手指上、电话上、门把手上都沾满了面团。\n[01:27.01]I had no sooner got back to the kitchen than the doorbell rang loud enough to wake the dead. | 我刚回到厨房，门铃就响了，声音大得足以把死人吵醒。\n[01:35.88]This time it was the postman and he wanted me to sign for a registered letter! | 这次是邮递员，他要我签收一封挂号信！",
