    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:A Blessing in Disguise?]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:11.01]Why does the vicar refuse to cut down the tree? | 为什么牧师拒绝砍掉这棵树？\n[00:16.94]The tiny village of Frinley is said to possess a 'cursed tree'. | 弗林利这个小村庄据说有一棵“被诅咒的树”。\n[00:22.89]Because the tree was mentioned in a newspaper, | 因为这棵树在报纸上被提及，\n[00:26.47]the number of visitors to Frinley has now increased. | 弗林利的游客数量现在增加了。\n[00:31.71]The tree was planted near the church fifty years ago, but it is only in recent years that it has gained an evil reputation. | 这棵树是五十年前种在教堂附近的，但直到最近几年才声名狼藉。\n[00:43.07]It is said that if anyone touches the tree, he will have bad luck; if he picks a leaf, he will die. | 据说如果任何人触摸这棵树，他就会有厄运；如果他摘一片叶子，他就会死去。\n[00:52.89]Many villagers believe that the tree has already claimed a number of victims. | 许多村民相信这棵树已经夺走了许多受害者的生命。\n[00:59.95]The vicar has been asked to have the tree cut down, but so far he has refused. | 牧师被要求砍掉这棵树，但到目前为止他一直拒绝。\n[01:08.52]He has pointed out that the tree is a useful source of income, | 他指出这棵树是一个有用的收入来源，\n[01:14.13]as tourists have been coming from all parts of the country to see it. | 因为游客们从全国各地赶来参观它。\n[01:20.04]In spite of all that has been said, | 尽管有各种说法，\n[01:23.23]the tourists have been picking leaves and cutting their names on the tree-trunk. | 游客们一直在摘叶子并在树干上刻下他们的名字。\n[01:29.10]So far, not one of them has been struck down by sudden death! | 到目前为止，他们中没有一个人被突然死亡击倒！",
