    "id": "us/NCE2/64.The Channel Tunnel",
    "book": "us",
    "group": "NCE2",
    "filename": "NCE2/64.The Channel Tunnel",
    "title": "The Channel Tunnel",
    "audioUrl": "NCE/NCE2/64.The Channel Tunnel.mp3",
    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE2/64.The Channel Tunnel.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:The Channel Tunnel]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.00]Why was the first tunnel not completed? | 为什么第一条隧道没有建成？\n[00:14.67]In 1858, a French engineer, Aime Thome de Gamond, | 1858年，一位名叫埃梅·托梅·德·加蒙的法国工程师，\n[00:20.80]arrived in England with a plan for a 21-mile tunnel under the English Channel. | 带着修建一条21英里长的英吉利海峡隧道的计划抵达英国。\n[00:27.69]He said that it would be possible to build a platform in the centre of the Channel. | 他说可以在海峡中央修建一个平台。\n[00:34.17]This platform would serve as a port and a railway station. | 这个平台将作为港口和火车站。\n[00:39.63]The tunnel would be well-ventilated if tall chimneys were built above sea level. | 如果在海平面以上修建高烟囱，隧道将能很好地通风。\n[00:46.35]In 1860, a better plan was put forward by an Englishman, William Low. | 1860年，英国人威廉·洛提出了一个更好的方案。\n[00:53.93]He suggested that a double railway-tunnel should be built. | 他建议修建一条双轨铁路隧道。\n[00:58.66]This would solve the problem of ventilation for if a train entered this tunnel, it would draw in fresh air behind it. | 这将解决通风问题，因为如果火车进入这条隧道，它会从后面吸入新鲜空气。\n[01:08.89]Forty-two years later a tunnel was actually begun. | 四十二年后，一条隧道实际开始动工。\n[01:13.97]If, at the time, the British had not feared invasion, it would have been completed. | 如果当时英国人没有害怕入侵，它就会建成。\n[01:22.13]The world had to wait almost another 100 years for the Channel Tunnel. | 世界不得不又等了将近100年才等到英吉利海峡隧道。\n[01:28.61]It was officially opened on March 7, 1994, finally connecting Britain to the European continent. | 它于1994年3月7日正式开通，最终将英国与欧洲大陆连接起来。",
