    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:Volcanoes]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.03]Why does Tazieff risk his life like this? | 为什么塔齐耶夫要这样冒生命危险？\n[00:15.75]Haroun Tazieff, the Polish scientist, has spent his lifetime studying active volcanoes and deep caves in all parts of the world. | 波兰科学家哈伦·塔齐耶夫一生都在研究世界各地的活火山和深洞。\n[00:27.85]In 1948, he went to Lake Kivu in the Congo to observe a new volcano which he later named Kituro. | 1948年，他去了刚果的基伍湖，观察一座新火山，他后来将其命名为基图罗。\n[00:39.75]Tazieff was able to set up his camp very close to the volcano while it was erupting violently. | 塔齐耶夫在火山猛烈喷发时，能够把营地设在离火山很近的地方。\n[00:49.28]Though he managed to take a number of brilliant photographs, he could not stay near the volcano for very long. | 尽管他设法拍了许多精彩的照片，但他不能在火山附近待太久。\n[00:58.83]He noticed that a river of liquid rock was coming towards him. | 他注意到一条液态岩石的河流正向他涌来。\n[01:03.93]It threatened to surround him completely, but Tazieff managed to escape just in time. | 它威胁要将他完全包围，但塔齐耶夫设法及时逃脱了。\n[01:12.79]He waited until the volcano became quiet and he was able to return two days later. | 他等到火山平静下来，两天后才得以返回。\n[01:20.47]This time, he managed to climb into the mouth of Kituro so that he could take photographs and measure temperatures. | 这次，他设法爬进了基图罗的火山口，以便拍照和测量温度。\n[01:30.92]Tazieff has often risked his life in this way. | 塔齐耶夫经常以这种方式冒生命危险。\n[01:35.69]He has been able to tell us more about active volcanoes than any man alive. | 他比任何在世的人都能告诉我们更多关于活火山的信息。",
