    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:Persistent]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.12]Why did Elizabeth tell Nigel that she was going to the dentist? | 伊丽莎白为什么告诉奈杰尔她要去看牙医？\n[00:17.62]I crossed the street to avoid meeting him but he saw me and came running towards me. | 我穿过街道，想避开他，但他看见了我，朝我跑过来。\n[00:25.25]It was no use pretending that I had not seen him, so I waved to him. | 假装没看见他也没用，所以我朝他挥了挥手。\n[00:32.56]I never enjoy meeting Nigel Dykes. | 我从不喜欢遇到奈杰尔·戴克斯。\n[00:36.76]He never has anything to do. | 他从没有什么事可做。\n[00:40.34]No matter how busy you are, he always insists on coming with you. | 不管你有多忙，他总是坚持要和你一起去。\n[00:47.77]I had to think of a way of preventing him from following me around all morning. | 我得想个办法阻止他整个上午跟着我。\n[00:54.80]'Hello, Nigel,' I said 'Fancy meeting you here!' | “你好，奈杰尔，”我说，“真巧在这儿见到你！”\n[01:00.59]'Hi, Elizabeth,' Nigel answered. 'I was just wondering how to spend the morning--until I saw you. | “嗨，伊丽莎白，”奈杰尔回答，“我刚才还在想怎么打发这个上午呢——直到我看见你。\n[01:10.77]You're not busy doing anything, are you?' | 你没什么事要做吧，是吗？”\n[01:14.56]'No, not at all,' I answered. 'I'm going to...' | “不，一点也不忙，”我回答，“我要去……”\n[01:19.86]'Would you mind my coming with you?' he asked, before I had finished speaking. | “你介意我跟你一起去吗？”他没等我说完就问道。\n[01:26.53]'Not at all,' I lied, 'but I'm going to the dentist.' | “一点也不，”我撒谎说，“不过我要去看牙医。”\n[01:32.57]'Then I'll come with you,' he answered. | “那我跟你一起去，”他回答道。\n[01:36.02]'There's always plenty to read in the waiting room!' | “候诊室里总是有很多东西可以读的！”",
