    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:But not Murder!]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:11.05]Do you think that the writer passed his driving test? Why? | 你认为作者通过驾照考试了吗？为什么？\n[00:18.03]I was being tested for a driving licence for the third time. | 我第三次参加驾驶执照考试。\n[00:23.38]I had been asked to drive in heavy traffic and had done so successfully. | 我被要求在车辆很多的道路上驾驶，并成功完成了。\n[00:30.18]After having been instructed to drive out of town, I began to acquire confidence. | 在被指示开出市区后，我开始有了信心。\n[00:37.95]Sure that I had passed, I was almost beginning to enjoy my test. | 确信我已通过，我几乎开始享受我的考试了。\n[00:45.04]The examiner must have been pleased with my performance, for he smiled and said, 'Just one more thing Mr. Eames. | 考官一定对我的表现很满意，因为他微笑着说：“还有一件事，伊姆斯先生。\n[00:55.66]Let us suppose that a child suddenly crosses the road in front of you. | 假设有个孩子突然从你车前跑过。\n[01:01.75]As soon as I tap on the window, you must stop within five feet.' | 我一敲车窗，你必须在五英尺内把车停住。”\n[01:08.32]I continued driving and after some time, the examiner tapped loudly. | 我继续驾驶，过了一会儿，考官大声敲击车窗。\n[01:14.64]Though the sound could be heard clearly, it took me a long time to react. | 尽管声音听得很清楚，但我过了好一会儿才做出反应。\n[01:21.62]I suddenly pressed the brake pedal hard and we were both thrown forward. | 我猛地踩下刹车踏板，结果我们俩都被猛地向前甩去。\n[01:27.64]The examiner looked at me sadly. | 考官悲伤地看着我。\n[01:31.22]'Mr. Eames,' he said, in a mournful voice, 'you have just killed that child!' | “伊姆斯先生，”他用悲哀的声音说，“你刚才把那个孩子撞死了！”",
