    "audioUrl": "NCE/NCE2/78.The Last One.mp3",
    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE2/78.The Last One.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:The Last One?]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:10.39]For how long did the writer give up smoking? | 作者戒烟戒了多久？\n[00:15.78]After reading an article entitled 'Cigarette Smoking and Your Health' I lit a cigarette to calm my nerves. | 读了一篇题为《吸烟与健康》的文章后，我点燃了一支香烟来镇定情绪。\n[00:26.25]I smoked with concentration and pleasure as I was sure that this would be my last cigarette. | 我聚精会神、津津有味地抽着，因为我确信这是我的最后一支香烟了。\n[00:35.11]For a whole week I did not smoke at all and during this time my wife suffered terribly. | 整整一个星期我根本没吸烟，在此期间我妻子可遭了大罪了。\n[00:43.84]I had all the usual symptoms of someone giving up smoking: a bad temper and an enormous appetite. | 我具备了戒烟者的所有常见症状：脾气暴躁，胃口大开。\n[00:53.83]My friends kept on offering me cigarettes and cigars. | 我的朋友们不断地给我递香烟和雪茄。\n[00:59.15]They made no effort to hide their amusement whenever I produced a packet of sweets from my pocket. | 每当我从口袋里掏出一包糖果时，他们都毫不掩饰地取笑我。\n[01:08.29]After seven days of this I went to a party. | 这样过了7天，我参加了一个聚会。\n[01:13.04]Everybody around me was smoking and I felt extremely uncomfortable. | 我周围的人都在吸烟，我感到非常不舒服。\n[01:19.78]When my old friend Brian urged me to accept a cigarette, it was more than I could bear. | 当我的老朋友布赖恩极力劝我抽一支烟时，我再也忍不住了。\n[01:29.23]I took one guiltily, lit it and smoked with satisfaction. | 我内疚地拿了一支，点上，心满意足地抽了起来。\n[01:35.71]My wife was delighted that things had returned to normal once more. | 我妻子很高兴一切又恢复了正常。\n[01:41.63]Anyway, as Brian pointed out, it is the easiest thing in the world to give up smoking. | 不过，正如布赖恩指出的，戒烟是世界上最容易的事情。\n[01:50.01]He himself has done it lots of times! | 他自己就戒过好多次了！",
    "hasAudio": true,
    "hasLrc": true,
    "source": "default"
