    "id": "us/NCE2/82.Monster or Fish",
    "book": "us",
    "group": "NCE2",
    "filename": "NCE2/82.Monster or Fish",
    "title": "Monster or Fish",
    "audioUrl": "NCE/NCE2/82.Monster or Fish.mp3",
    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE2/82.Monster or Fish.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:Monster or Fish?]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:11.44]What was the monster called? | 那个怪物叫什么名字？\n[00:15.27]Fishermen and sailors sometimes claim to have seen monsters in the sea. | 渔民和水手有时声称在海中见过怪物。\n[00:21.92]Though people have often laughed at stories told by seamen, | 尽管人们常常嘲笑水手们讲述的故事，\n[00:27.10]it is now known that many of these 'monsters' which have at times been sighted are simply strange fish. | 但现在已知，这些有时被目击到的“怪物”很多只是奇怪的鱼。\n[00:36.82]Occasionally, unusual creatures are washed to the shore, but they are rarely caught out at sea. | 偶尔，不寻常的生物会被冲到岸边，但它们很少在海上被捕获。\n[00:45.77]Some time ago, however, a peculiar fish was caught near Madagascar. | 然而，不久前，一条奇特的鱼在马达加斯加附近被捕获。\n[00:53.36]A small fishing boat was carried miles out to sea by the powerful fish as it pulled on the line. | 当这条强壮的鱼拉扯鱼线时，一艘小渔船被拖离海岸数英里。\n[01:02.23]Realizing that this was no ordinary fish, the fisherman made every effort not to damage it in any way. | 渔民意识到这不是一条普通的鱼，便竭尽全力不损坏它。\n[01:13.66]When it was eventually brought to shore, it was found to be over thirteen feet long. | 当它最终被带到岸上时，发现它有十三英尺多长。\n[01:21.91]It had a head like a horse big blue eyes, shining silver skin, and a bright red tail. | 它有一个像马一样的头，大大的蓝眼睛，闪亮的银色皮肤和一条鲜红的尾巴。\n[01:31.54]The fish, which has since been set to a museum where it is being examined by a scientist, is called an oarfish. | 这条鱼后来被送往博物馆，由科学家进行研究，它被称为皇带鱼。\n[01:41.93]Such creatures have rarely been seen alive by man as they live at a depth of six hundred feet. | 这种生物很少被人类活体发现，因为它们生活在六百英尺深的地方。",
    "hasAudio": true,
    "hasLrc": true,
    "source": "default"
