    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:A Perfect Alibi]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:11.31]What was wrong with the man's story? | 这个人的话有什么漏洞？\n[00:16.13]'At the time the murder was committed, I was travelling on the 8 o'clock train to London,' said the man. | “在谋杀发生的时候，我正坐8点钟的火车去伦敦。”那人说。\n[00:25.96]'Do you always catch such an early train?' asked the inspector. | “你总是赶这么早的火车吗？”探长问。\n[00:31.71]'Of course I do,' answered the man. | “我当然是。”那人回答。\n[00:35.86]'I must be at work at 10 o'clock. | “我10点钟必须上班。\n[00:39.00]My employer will confirm that I was there on time.' | 我的雇主可以证明我准时到了那里。”\n[00:44.69]'Would a later train get you to work on time?' asked the inspector. | “晚一点的火车也能让你准时上班吗？”探长问。\n[00:51.08]'I suppose it would, but I never catch a later train.' | “我想是的，但我从不赶晚一点的火车。”\n[00:57.15]'At what time did you arrive at the station?' | “你什么时候到车站的？”\n[01:02.05]'At ten to eight. I bought a paper and waited for the train.' | “7点50分。我买了一份报纸，然后等火车。”\n[01:08.08]'And you didn't notice anything unusual?' | “你没注意到什么不寻常的事情吗？”\n[01:13.13]'Of course not.' | “当然没有。”\n[01:15.68]'I suggest,' said the inspector,' that you are not telling the truth. | “我猜想，”探长说，“你没有说实话。\n[01:22.98]I suggest that you did not catch the 8 o'clock train, | 我猜想你并没有赶上8点钟的火车，\n[01:27.84]but that you caught the 8.25 which would still get you to work on time. | 而是赶了8点25分的火车，那也能让你准时上班。\n[01:34.87]You see, on the morning of the murder, the 8 o'clock train did not run at all. | 你看，在谋杀发生的那天早上，8点钟的火车根本就没有开。\n[01:42.66]It broke down at Ferngreen station and was taken off the line.' | 它在弗恩格林车站出了故障，被拉下了线路。”",
    "hasAudio": true,
