    "title": "Future Champions",
    "audioUrl": "NCE/NCE2/94.Future Champions.mp3",
    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE2/94.Future Champions.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:Future Champions]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:11.29]What kind of race do the children compete in? | 孩子们参加的是哪种比赛？\n[00:16.63]Experiments have proved that children can be instructed in swimming at a very early age. | 实验证明，孩子们可以在很小的时候就被教导游泳。\n[00:25.10]At a special swimming pool in Los Angeles, | 在洛杉矶的一个特殊游泳池里，\n[00:28.72]children become expert at holding their breath under water even before they can walk. | 孩子们甚至在学会走路之前就能熟练地在水下憋气。\n[00:36.50]Babies of two months old do not appear to be reluctant to enter the water. | 两个月大的婴儿似乎并不抵触下水。\n[00:42.95]It is not long before they are so accustomed to swimming that they can pick up weights from the floor of the pool. | 没过多久，他们就非常适应游泳了，甚至能从泳池底部捡起重物。\n[00:51.71]A game that is very popular with these young swimmers is the underwater tricycle race. | 这些小泳者非常喜欢的一项游戏是水下三轮车比赛。\n[00:59.56]Tricycles are lined up on the floor of the pool seven feet under water. | 三轮车排成一列，放置在水下七英尺深的泳池底部。\n[01:06.26]The children compete against each other to reach the other end of the pool. | 孩子们互相竞争，看谁先到达泳池的另一端。\n[01:12.26]Many pedal their tricycles but most of them prefer to push or drag them. | 许多孩子会蹬他们的三轮车，但大多数人更喜欢推或拖它们。\n[01:19.68]Some children can cover the whole length of the pool without coming up for breath even once. | 有些孩子甚至可以游完整个泳池的长度而不用浮出水面换气一次。\n[01:28.12]Whether they will ever become future Olympic champions, only time will tell. | 他们将来是否会成为奥运冠军，只有时间能证明。\n[01:34.50]Meanwhile, they should encourage those among us who cannot swim five yards before they are gasping for air. | 同时，他们应该鼓励我们中那些游不到五码就气喘吁吁的人。",
