    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE2/95.A Fantasy.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第二册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:A Fantasy]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:09.57]Why was the Ambassador particularly lucky? | 为什么大使特别幸运？\n[00:14.92]When the Ambassador of Escalopia returned home for lunch, his wife got a shock. | 当埃斯卡洛皮亚大使回家吃午饭时，他的妻子吓了一跳。\n[00:23.22]He looked pale and his clothes were in a frightful state. | 他脸色苍白，衣服也糟透了。\n[00:28.74]'What has happened?' she asked. | “出什么事了？”她问道。\n[00:32.77]'How did your clothes get into such a mess?' | “你的衣服怎么搞得这么乱？”\n[00:37.81]'A fire extinguisher, my dear,' answered the Ambassador drily. | “灭火器，亲爱的，”大使干巴巴地回答道。\n[00:43.66]'University students set the Embassy on fire this morning.' | “今天早上大学生把大使馆点着了。”\n[00:48.63]'Good heavens!' exclaimed his wife. | “天哪！”他的妻子惊呼道。\n[00:52.87]'And where were you at the time?' | “那你当时在哪里？”\n[00:56.61]'I was in my office as usual,' answered the Ambassador. | “我像往常一样在办公室里，”大使回答道。\n[01:01.45]'The fire broke out in the basement. | “火灾发生在地下室。\n[01:04.41]I went down immediately, of course, and that fool, Horst, | 我当然立刻下去了，然后那个傻瓜霍斯特，\n[01:09.87]aimed a fire extinguisher at me. | 把灭火器对准了我。\n[01:12.80]He thought I was on fire. | 他以为我着火了。\n[01:15.67]I must definitely get that fellow posted.' | 我一定要把那个家伙调走。”\n[01:20.33]The Ambassador's wife went on asking questions, | 大使夫人继续提问，\n[01:24.40]when she suddenly noticed a big hole in her husband's hat. | 突然她发现丈夫的帽子上有一个大洞。\n[01:30.27]'And how can you explain that?' she asked. | “那你怎么解释那个？”她问道。\n[01:34.88]'Oh, that,' said the Ambassador. | “哦，那个，”大使说道。\n[01:38.56]'Someone fired a shot through my office window. | “有人朝我办公室窗户开了一枪。\n[01:42.59]Accurate, don't you think? | 够准的，不是吗？\n[01:44.88]Fortunately, I wasn't wearing it at the time. | 幸好，我当时没戴着它。\n[01:49.36]If I had been, I would not have been able to get home for lunch.' | 如果我当时戴着，我就不能回家吃午饭了。”",
    "hasAudio": true,
