    "id": "us/NCE3/03.An Unknown Goddess",
    "book": "us",
    "group": "NCE3",
    "filename": "NCE3/03.An Unknown Goddess",
    "title": "An Unknown Goddess",
    "audioUrl": "NCE/NCE3/03.An Unknown Goddess.mp3",
    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE3/03.An Unknown Goddess.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第三册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:An Unknown Goddess]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:00.95]Lesson 3 | 第3课\n[00:02.34]An unknown goddess | 一个不知名的女神\n[00:10.64]How did the archaeologists know that the statue was a goddess? | 考古学家怎么知道这座雕像是女神？\n[00:16.23]Some time ago, an interesting discovery was made by archaeologists on the Aegean island of Kea. | 不久前，考古学家在爱琴海的凯阿岛上有一项有趣的发现。\n[00:24.33]An American team explored a temple which stands in an ancient city on the promontory of Ayia Irini. | 一个美国小组考察了在阿伊亚伊里尼海角的一座古城中的一座神庙。\n[00:32.71]The city at one time must have been prosperous, for it enjoyed a high level of civilization. | 这座城市曾一度繁荣，因为它享有高度的文明。\n[00:38.98]Houses -- often three storeys high -- were built of stone. | 房屋——通常有三层楼高——是用石头建造的。\n[00:44.07]They had large rooms with beautifully decorated walls. | 它们有大房间，墙壁装饰精美。\n[00:48.39]The city was even equipped with a drainage system, for a great many clay pipes were found beneath the narrow streets. | 这座城市甚至配备了排水系统，因为在狭窄的街道下发现了大量的陶土管道。\n[00:57.46]The temple which the archaeologists explored was used as a place of worship from the fifteenth century B.C. until Roman times. | 考古学家考察的神庙从公元前15世纪一直到罗马时代都被用作礼拜场所。\n[01:07.15]In the most sacred room of the temple, clay fragments of fifteen statues were found. | 在神庙最神圣的房间里，发现了15尊雕像的陶土碎片。\n[01:14.21]Each of these represented a goddess and had, at one time, been painted. | 每一尊都代表一位女神，并且曾被涂上颜色。\n[01:20.18]The body of one statue was found among remains dating from the 15th century B.C. | 一尊雕像的身体是在可追溯到公元前15世纪的遗迹中发现的。\n[01:27.02]Its missing head happened to be among remains of the fifth century B.C. | 它缺失的头部碰巧在公元前5世纪的遗迹中。\n[01:32.80]This head must have been found in Classical times and carefully preserved. | 这个头部一定是在古典时期被发现并精心保存下来的。\n[01:37.84]It was very old and precious even then. | 即使在当时，它也非常古老而珍贵。\n[01:41.87]When the archaeologists reconstructed the fragments, they were amazed to find that the goddess turned out to be a very modern-looking woman. | 当考古学家重组这些碎片时，他们惊讶地发现这位女神竟然是一个看起来非常现代的女人。\n[01:51.07]She stood three feet high and her hands rested on her hips. | 她身高三英尺，双手叉腰。\n[01:55.76]She was wearing a full-length skirt which swept the ground. | 她穿着一件拖地的长裙。\n[01:59.95]Despite her great age, she was very graceful indeed, but, so far, the archaeologists have been unable to discover her identity. | 尽管她年代久远，但确实非常优雅，不过到目前为止，考古学家们还未能发现她的身份。",
    "hasAudio": true,
    "hasLrc": true,
    "source": "default"
