    "filename": "NCE4/44.Patterns of Culture",
    "title": "Patterns of Culture",
    "audioUrl": "NCE/NCE4/44.Patterns of Culture.mp3",
    "lrcUrl": "NCE/NCE4/44.Patterns of Culture.lrc",
    "lrcText": "[al:新概念英语第四册]\n[ar:山海作品推荐]\n[ti:Patterns of Culture]\n[by:山海作品推荐]\n[00:00.78]Lesson 44 | 第44课\n[00:02.62]Patterns of culture | 文化的模式\n[00:09.88]What influences us from the moment of birth? | 从我们出生那一刻起，什么在影响着我们？\n[00:15.46]Custom has not commonly been regarded as a subject of any great moment. | 习俗通常不被认为是一个举足轻重的问题。\n[00:20.81]The inner workings of our own brains we feel to be uniquely worthy of investigation, | 我们认为我们自己大脑的内部运作是独一无二地值得研究的，\n[00:26.82]but custom, we have a way of thinking, is behaviour at is most commonplace. | 但我们有一种想法，认为习俗是最常见的行为。\n[00:33.35]As a matter of fact, it is the other way around. | 事实上，情况恰恰相反。\n[00:36.88]Traditional custom, taken the world over, | 传统的习俗，遍布世界各地，\n[00:39.96]is a mass of detailed behaviour more astonishing than what any one person can ever evolve in individual actions, | 是一堆详细的行为，比任何个人在单独行动中所能演变出的行为都更令人惊讶，\n[00:48.53]no matter how aberrant. | 无论多么反常。\n[00:50.73]Yet that is a rather trivial aspect of the matter. | 然而，这只是问题的微不足道的一面。\n[00:54.70]The fact of first-rate importance is the predominant role that custom plays in experience and in belief, | 最重要的事实是习俗在经验和信仰中扮演的主导角色，\n[01:02.52]and the very great varieties it may manifest. | 以及它可能表现出的巨大多样性。\n[01:07.28]No man ever looks at the world with pristine eyes. | 没有人能以纯粹的眼光看待世界。\n[01:11.45]He sees it edited by a definite set of customs and institutions and ways of thinking. | 他看到的世界是由一套明确的习俗、制度和思维方式所塑造的。\n[01:18.15]Even in his philosophical probings he cannot go behind these stereotypes; | 即使在他的哲学探索中，他也无法超越这些刻板印象；\n[01:23.66]his very concepts of the true and the false will still have reference to his particular traditional customs. | 他对真与假的观念仍然会与他特定的传统习俗相关联。\n[01:31.50]John Dewey has said in all seriousness that the part played by custom in shaping the behaviour of the individual, | 约翰·杜威曾非常严肃地说，习俗在塑造个人行为中所起的作用，\n[01:39.36]as against any way in which he can affect traditional custom, | 与他能够影响传统习俗的任何方式相比，\n[01:43.65]is as the proportion of the total vocabulary of his mother tongue | 就像他母语的全部词汇量，\n[01:48.64]against those words of his own baby talk that are taken up into the vernacular of his family. | 与他自己咿呀学语中被家庭口语采纳的词语之比。\n[01:56.17]When one seriously studies the social orders that have had the opportunity to develop autonomously, | 当人们认真研究那些有机会自主发展的社会秩序时，\n[02:03.58]the figure becomes no more than an exact and matter-of-fact observation. | 这个比喻就成了精确而实际的观察。\n[02:09.12]The life history of the individual is first and foremost an accommodation | 个体的生命历程首先是一种适应，\n[02:14.42]to the patterns and standards traditionally handed down in his community. | 适应其社区中世代相传的模式和标准。\n[02:20.21]From the moment of his birth, | 从他出生那一刻起，\n[02:22.20]the customs into which he is born shape his experience and behaviour. | 他所降生的习俗塑造了他的经验和行为。\n[02:27.53]By the time he can talk, he is the little creature of his culture, | 等到他会说话时，他已是其文化的小小产物，\n[02:32.38]and by the time he is grown and able to take part in its activities, | 等到他长大成人并能参与其活动时，\n[02:37.30]its habits are his habits, its beliefs his beliefs, its impossibilities his impossibilities. | 它的习惯是他的习惯，它的信仰是他的信仰，它的不可能之事是他的不可能之事。\n[02:45.92]Every child that is born into his group will share them with him, | 每一个出生在他群体中的孩子都会与他分享这些，\n[02:50.38]and no child born into one on the opposite side of the globe can ever achieve the thousandth part. | 而出生在地球另一边的孩子连千分之一也无法做到。\n[02:57.64]There is no social problem it is more incumbent upon us to understand than this of the role of custom. | 没有比理解习俗的作用更重要的社会问题了。\n[03:05.73]Until we are intelligent as to its laws and varieties, | 在我们对其规律和多样性有充分了解之前，\n[03:09.78]the main complicating facts of human life must remain unintelligible. | 人类生活的主要复杂事实必然是难以理解的。\n[03:15.99]The study of custom can be profitable only after certain preliminary propositions have been accepted, | 对习俗的研究只有在某些初步命题被接受之后才能有所裨益，\n[03:23.68]and some of these propositions have been violently opposed. | 而其中一些命题曾遭到强烈反对。\n[03:28.49]In the first place, any scientific study requires that there be no | 首先，任何科学研究都要求，\n[03:33.38]preferential weighting of one or another of the items in the series it selects for its consideration. | 在它所选择的系列项目进行考量时，不应对其中任何一项有偏向性地加权。\n[03:40.88]In all the less controversial fields, like the study of cacti or termites or the nature of nebulae, | 在所有争议较少的领域，比如研究仙人掌、白蚁或星云的性质，\n[03:48.21]the necessary method of study is to group the relevant material and to take note of all possible variant forms and conditions. | 必要的研究方法是将相关材料分组，并记录所有可能的变体形式和条件。\n[03:56.75]In this way, we have learned all that we know of the laws of astronomy, or of the habits of the social insects, let us say. | 通过这种方式，我们掌握了天文学的所有规律，或者说，掌握了群居昆虫的习性。\n[04:06.01]It is only in the study of man himself that the major social sciences | 只有在研究人类自身时，主要的社会科学才\n[04:11.19]have substituted the study of one local variation, that of Western civilization. | 将对西方文明这一地方性变体的研究取而代之。\n[04:18.21]Anthropology was by definition impossible, | 人类学按定义来说是不可能的，\n[04:21.58]as long as these distinctions between ourselves and the primitive, | 只要我们与原始人、\n[04:26.14]ourselves and the barbarian, ourselves and the pagan, held sway over people's minds. | 我们与野蛮人、我们与异教徒之间的这些区别仍然主宰着人们的思想。\n[04:32.65]It was necessary first to arrive at that degree of sophistication | 首先，有必要达到那种成熟程度，\n[04:37.42]where we no longer set our own belief against our neighbour's superstition. | 即我们不再将自己的信仰与邻居的迷信对立起来。\n[04:42.42]It was necessary to recognize that these institutions which are based on the same premises, let us say the supernatural, | 有必要认识到，这些基于相同前提的制度，比方说超自然现象，\n[04:51.74]must be considered together, our own among the rest. | 必须被一并考虑，包括我们自己的。",
    "hasAudio": true,
    "hasLrc": true,
    "source": "default"
